Fill in each section for your commands, then delete each line that starts with "Fill:".

## Prerequisites

- `just acceptance` passes on the fixture that [spec.md](spec.md#acceptance) names in `## Acceptance`, in a clone at the tested tag
- `python3` 3.9 or later, which the example command runs
- `wc`, for the independent check

Fill: each program that the extension wraps, at the version that `vision.md` names as tested, and each tool of the independent check.

## Prompt for the fresh agent

"Use Nicely to count the lines of `<run>/notes.md`"

Fill: one sentence that a user would say, without a command, a flag, or a hint.

## Criteria

| Family | Criterion | Covered by |
|---|---|---|
| Result | `wc -c` gives the `size_bytes` of the answer | `just acceptance` |
| Fidelity | The answer keeps the properties that [spec.md](spec.md#acceptance) names in `## Acceptance` | `just acceptance`, which claims the spec ID of each property |
| Determinism | Runs on one host give the same answer | `just acceptance`, which runs the command twice |
| Errors | Each line of Failures and each refusal of `## Acceptance` in [spec.md](spec.md) gives its code | The test that claims its spec ID, which the test kit requires. The replay of [Error cases](#error-cases) on the host |
| Uninstall | The steps of [Uninstall](#uninstall) | `just acceptance`, on its scratch install |

Fill: for each family, what a tool other than the extension measures on the output.

Fill: in Covered by, the test that proves the criterion. When no test can, write `Manual:` and the reason, such as a screen that only a human sees.

## Error cases

Run each case as a run, and as a dry run when the command has one. A dry run gives the code of the run for each case of the shared preparation. The line of [spec.md](spec.md) that the spec ID names holds the expected code. `exit-codes.md` of the contract, in the folder that `just contract` prints, gives the exit code of each code.

| Case | spec.md | Expected, in addition to the code |
|---|---|---|
| A missing path, a symbolic link to one, or `--timeout soon` | `bad-input` | The message names the path or the value |
| A symbolic link to the input | None | The answer for the file that the link names |
| A `--timeout` that expires, such as `1s` on a long run | `worker-fails` | The wrapped program stops |
| Ctrl-C during the run | `interrupted` | The wrapped program stops |
| SIGTERM during the run | `terminated` | The wrapped program stops |
| An image, such as a PNG | `not-text` | The message names the file |

Fill: for a command that writes, the cases of its output, such as an existing output without `--force`, and a read-only output folder. After each case, the output does not change.

Fill: a row for each refusal of `## Acceptance` in [spec.md](spec.md#acceptance).

## Uninstall

1. After the last run, run `just uninstall` in the clone.
2. Run `ncly describe {{ root }} --json`. It answers `NOT_FOUND`, exit 2.

Removal keeps the keys and the grants, as [Release and install](https://github.com/pascalandy/nicely/blob/main/docs/north-star/contract/extensions.md#release-and-install) says.

## Known limits

[spec.md](spec.md) holds each accepted limit. A limit never contradicts a line of Failures or of Acceptance.

Fill: each defect that a UAT found and that is still open, with its issue.

## Gotchas

- Scratch XDG folders break a `just` that mise installed, because its shim then reads the config, state, and installs of mise there. Run `mise which just` before you move them, and call that path. `just acceptance` finds each program first.

Fill: each surprise that the next tester must know, such as the time of one run on the test host.
